-- הסכם אופק חדש (25.12.2008), §65 שכר מנהלים חדשים: a new principal in a
-- reform school is paid by the principals' table (annex י"ב), updated as
-- §35(ב); placed at grade 1 by the school's complexity level, a full-time
-- grade-1 principal earning at least 12,200 ₪ at the start of תשס"ט and
-- 12,383 ₪ in the December 2008 salary; a reform teacher appointed
-- principal goes to the grade whose salary is nearest at or above his last
-- table salary with role allowances; a teacher off the reform appointed in
-- a reform school, by the conversion of §§44–45; and one appointed where
-- the reform is not applied stays on the existing agreements.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `65 שכר מנהלים חדשים`

-- (א): the principals' table is annex י"ב, which the corpus does not publish
-- with the agreement: an input by complexity level and grade (the grades
-- and intermediate grades of (ד)(2) as its rows), updated as §35(ב).
@ref akn:art_65__para_a
ASSUME `the principals' table` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER AND NUMBER TO NUMBER

-- (ב): grade 1 at the school's level; the floor of a full-time grade-1
-- principal's pay.
@ref akn:art_65__para_b
GIVEN `salary day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a grade-1 principal's least pay` `salary day` IS
    BRANCH IF `salary day` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008) THEN 12383
           IF `salary day` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2008) THEN 12200
           OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `table value` IS A NUMBER, `salary day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a new grade-1 principal's full-time pay` `table value` `salary day` IS
    max `table value` (`a grade-1 principal's least pay` `salary day`)

-- The grade among those offered whose pay is the nearest at or above a
-- target: the least pay not below it.
GIVEN target IS A NUMBER, `pay at each grade` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the pay of the grade nearest at or above` target `pay at each grade` IS
    listToMaybe (sort (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p AT LEAST target) `pay at each grade`))

-- (ג): a reform teacher appointed principal: the target is his last table
-- salary with the role allowances he had on the eve of the appointment.
@ref akn:art_65__para_c
GIVEN `last table salary` IS A NUMBER, `role allowances on the eve` IS A NUMBER, `pay at each grade` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `a reform teacher's pay as principal` `last table salary` `role allowances on the eve` `pay at each grade` IS
    `the pay of the grade nearest at or above` (`last table salary` PLUS `role allowances on the eve`) `pay at each grade`

-- (ד): a teacher off the reform appointed in a reform school: (1) his pay
-- converted (A) by §§44–45 (an input until they are encoded); (2) the grade
-- or intermediate grade nearest at or above A.
@ref akn:art_65__para_d akn:art_65__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_65__para_d__subpara_2
GIVEN `A, the converted pay` IS A NUMBER, `pay at each grade and intermediate grade` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `a converted teacher's pay as principal` `A, the converted pay` `pay at each grade and intermediate grade` IS
    `the pay of the grade nearest at or above` `A, the converted pay` `pay at each grade and intermediate grade`

-- (ה): appointed where the reform is not applied, the existing agreements
-- go on until it is.
@ref akn:art_65__para_e
GIVEN `on the reform` IS A BOOLEAN, `the school applies the reform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `stays on the existing agreements as principal` `on the reform` `the school applies the reform` IF
    (NOT `on the reform`) AND (NOT `the school applies the reform`)

-- Placeholder rows of a complexity level: 12,000, 12,600, 13,300.
#ASSERT `a reform teacher's pay as principal` 11000 1000 (LIST 12000, 12600, 13300) EQUALS JUST 12000
#ASSERT `a reform teacher's pay as principal` 11000 1100 (LIST 12000, 12600, 13300) EQUALS JUST 12600
#ASSERT `a new grade-1 principal's full-time pay` 12000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2008) EQUALS 12200
#ASSERT `a new grade-1 principal's full-time pay` 12000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008) EQUALS 12383
#ASSERT NOT `stays on the existing agreements as principal` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `stays on the existing agreements as principal` FALSE FALSE
